# Financial Year Business Rules

- Only one ACTIVE Financial Year
- Name must be unique
- Start Date must be before End Date
- Closed Financial Years are read-only
- no overlay with existing end and start date while creating a new financial year
- Closing requires reconciliation
- Active Financial Years must not overlap according to business rules

# Financial Year phases
1. Create a financial year with start and end date and remarks
2. Assign members to it. Members will have existing loan, initial 
3. Select Executive committe from the memebers
4. Update bank balance, cash in hand, excess corpus, other investments, other loans
5. Summary will display total contribution of memebers, total loan adding each memebr's loan, bank balance, cash balance, excess corpus etc. 
6. Summary tab will have a start financial year button
7. States - Draft, in progress, validate, approved, closed
8. Each feature of financial year will be separate tabs


